WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:16.330
From a watch list
on the monitor tab,

2
00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:18.100
click the underlying
symbol you wish

3
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.530
to create your options trade for.

4
00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:23.670
So long as your tabs are part
of the same Windows group,

5
00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:27.040
the underlying will appear
in the order entry panel.

6
00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:29.305
To the right of the
order entry panel,

7
00:00:29.305 --> 00:00:32.395
select option chain from
the drop-down menu.

8
00:00:32.395 --> 00:00:35.560
The option chain display
shows call options to

9
00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.240
the left and put options to

10
00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:39.985
the right of the
central strike column.

11
00:00:39.985 --> 00:00:42.730
You will see the price
and daily change of

12
00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:45.605
the underlying to the
upper right of the window.

13
00:00:45.605 --> 00:00:47.225
Above the col area,

14
00:00:47.225 --> 00:00:49.940
you will see tabs for
different expirations.

15
00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:53.750
Click a tab or to locate
additional expiration dates,

16
00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:55.945
click on the ''More'' tab.

17
00:00:55.945 --> 00:00:57.770
Above the port area,

18
00:00:57.770 --> 00:01:00.755
you will see a dropdown
menu for strike prices.

19
00:01:00.755 --> 00:01:03.560
Access this menu to change or

20
00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:07.160
refine the number of strike
prices displayed on the page.

21
00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:09.020
Hovering the cursor above

22
00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:11.885
any bid price displays
a red background.

23
00:01:11.885 --> 00:01:14.885
This indicates that by
clicking on the field,

24
00:01:14.885 --> 00:01:18.155
it would create an order
to sell that option.

25
00:01:18.155 --> 00:01:20.480
Hovering above any asked price,

26
00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.040
displays a blue background

27
00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:24.335
indicating that by
clicking on this field,

28
00:01:24.335 --> 00:01:27.425
it would create an
audit to buy an option.

29
00:01:27.425 --> 00:01:29.390
Clicking a single strike will

30
00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:31.265
close the option chain window and

31
00:01:31.265 --> 00:01:33.005
populates the order entry panel

32
00:01:33.005 --> 00:01:35.195
with the chosen option leg.

33
00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:39.245
Locate the desired option
strike you want to transact.

34
00:01:39.245 --> 00:01:41.360
Click on the relevant
price field,

35
00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:44.225
which will close the
option chain display.

36
00:01:44.225 --> 00:01:46.070
Use the order entry panel to

37
00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:48.695
define the quantity
of options to trade.

38
00:01:48.695 --> 00:01:52.445
Choose the right order type
from the drop down menu.

39
00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:54.560
If using a limit price,

40
00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:56.210
choose the value by clicking in

41
00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:59.320
the input field or simply
typing in the value.

42
00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:02.115
Select from the time
enforced drop down,

43
00:02:02.115 --> 00:02:04.680
whether this is a
day or GTC order.

44
00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:06.375
Your order is ready to review.

45
00:02:06.375 --> 00:02:07.835
Click the ''Submit'' button

46
00:02:07.835 --> 00:02:10.250
to generate an
order confirmation.

47
00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:13.910
When you have reviewed the
details, click ''transmit''.

48
00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:15.860
The order is sent for execution

49
00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:17.420
at the exchange
and will appear in

50
00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:21.020
the activity panel to the
lower left of mosaic.

51
00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:23.980
To pause or interact
with an act of order,

52
00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:25.760
click on it in the activity panel

53
00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:28.320
and make the relevant choice.